{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131179-immediate-nimbus-tilts","id":1131179,"title":"Immediate Nimbus Tilts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-19T04:13:20-07:00","id":1131179,"title":"Immediate Nimbus Tilts","content":"So, I am creating a massive, &quot;free-roaming&quot; sandboxy campaign for Vampire the Requiem in Cologne. I naturally put some other creatures here and there, that\u00b4s why I\u00b4m scanning the other books and make someother creatures, in this case: Mages.<br /> <br /> I am a bit confused about the tilts in the immediate Nimbus Flare. So, basically it\u00b4s a cosmetic thing, glowing auras, smells, glowing tatoos that are only visible with mage sight- But it also reads that it does a tilt &quot;unique to a character&quot;. As I can find a list of these tilts, I assume I should make a tilt of my own. So, how strong is it?<br /> <br /> Say, I got a gothic Acanthus here. When she flares, you can see all the other possibilities she could have been (you see her as a surgeon for a moment, that blends over in a prostitute, blends over to a Tai boxer etc).<br /> Now to the tilt: When her Gnosis is higher than your Resolve, you get a revelation of what you could have been. For the rest of the scene or when you spent a Willpower point, you get -2 if you do something that fits your alternate self, or get +2 if you do something that fits your other future.<br /> <br /> Is that meant by the tilt you get?<br /> <br /> Thx for the help and keep on gaming,<br /> <br /> Dennis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T04:26:57-07:00","id":1131180,"title":"","content":"The tilt is a short lived dice effect that's equal to half their Gnosis rounded up. For example, My effective Gnosis 5 (due to a merit that increases it by 3) let's my character's Nimbus of a strong sense of oncoming doom (as Acanthus) cause -1 to Resolve and Composure, but increase Defense by 1. Does that help at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T04:57:08-07:00","id":1131671,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah. This helps actually quite a lot. I just haven\u00b4t time by actually reading all the books for a few NPCs, and it seems that I missed that guidelines.<br /> <br /> But further: Would my tilt I mentioned above work? Say, she has Gnosis 4. Could it cause -2 to her next die roll if the affected character does something &quot;against his destiny&quot; and +2 if he does something fitting to his &quot;should have been&quot;. Would that fit?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T05:31:36-07:00","id":1131672,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly (and I might not, because we ditched the Nimbus Tilt system), you pick a skill or trait, decide if it's a bonus or a malus, and that's it. <br /> If you have access to Hurt Locker, it has a system for modifying scenes using something akin to &quot;scene tilts&quot;, and I feel that it would work better with what Nimbus Tilts tried to achieve than Personal Tilt system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:41:46-07:00","id":1131703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131179-immediate-nimbus-tilts?p=1131671#post1131671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah. This helps actually quite a lot. I just haven\u00b4t time by actually reading all the books for a few NPCs, and it seems that I missed that guidelines.<br /> <br /> But further: Would my tilt I mentioned above work? Say, she has Gnosis 4. Could it cause -2 to her next die roll if the affected character does something &quot;against his destiny&quot; and +2 if he does something fitting to his &quot;should have been&quot;. Would that fit?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help-</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW this does not work that way. But you can easily make it work that way and it doesn't seem particularily overpowered to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:11:54-07:00","id":1131738,"title":"","content":"So, I checked it, and yeah: in Hurt Locker, you get something called Framing Scenes. The way Scene is Framed allows characters to use it for Advantage (+2), or act against it and suffer a penalty (-2), while also adding a scene specific consequence to Dramatic Failures. This works much closer to what you want to do, so I would suggest switching from the corebook Nimbus to Immediate Nimbus reframing the scene accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}